The change does what #1207 asked. There is now one function that decides the highest temperature per provider:
• 2.0: openai, google, deepseek, groq and cerebras. Each has a link to its API reference in a comment.
• 1.0: everything else, including anthropic and any unknown or custom server. The code also says why xai, zai, openrouter and mistral stay at 1.0.

All the places that read temperature now use that one function: the startup clamp, every agent build (so a fallback or /provider switch clamps again to the new provider's range), /config set and config get/config show.

